ps://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026-27 Week 11 College Football Playoff, bowl projections","description":"Our bowl gurus take a look at how the postseason picture shifted after Week 11.","published":"2026-11-16T12:28:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50473016/2026-week-11-college-football-playoff-bowl-projections","type":"Story","byline":"Kyle Bonagura and Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"College football takeaways: Lasting impressions from Week 11","description":"Our college football experts break down the most important things they saw in Week 11.","published":"2026-11-16T12:21:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/mondaytakeaways111626/2026-college-football-takeaways-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922981/rasheem-biles","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rasheem_Biles"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Rasheem Biles","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rasheem_Biles","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:23Z","intro":"Rasheem Biles (born November 18, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Texas Longhorns. He previously played for the Pittsburgh Panthers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Biles attended Pickerington High School Central in Pickerington, Ohio, where he played wide receiver, running back and defensive back. As a senior he played in five games due to injury and had over 400 all-purpose yards and five total touchdowns including two interceptions returned for touchdown. As a junior he had 74 tackles and three interceptions with two returned for a touchdown. Biles committed to the University of Pittsburgh to play college."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"PITTSBURGH\nAs a true freshman at Pittsburgh in 2023, Biles played in nine games and tied a school record with three blocked punts. He became a starter his sophomore year in 2024, starting nine of 12 games and recording 82 tackles, 5.5 sacks and an interception which he returned for a touchdown. He returned to Pittsburgh as a starter in 2025, playing in 10 games and recording 101 tackles, 4.5 sacks, two interceptions, both returned for touchdowns, two forced fumbles, and one fumble recovery, returned for a touchdown. At the end of the season, Biles entered the transfer portal.\n\nTEXAS\nOn January 10, 2026, Biles committed to Texas. In Week 9 against Mississippi State, Biles recorded eight tackles, including three sacks and four tackles for a loss, and two forced fumbles, earning SEC Co-Defensive Player of the Week for his performance."}]}}